# The guard of board-keeps-drafts.drive, for a view brought to the front. tests/drive.rs
# installs the open-tasks example patched to send view/show for its list whenever the tasks
# change. The list is opened first, and Enter on a canvas's task puts the whiteboard in front
# of it. While a card is typed there, a task another program writes makes the extension ask:
# the card stays, and when the edit ends the status line says what was not done. The notice
# is the board's, so the menu doesn't repeat it after q. With nothing unsaved, the next
# view/show brings the list to the front.
size 140x30
env COLD_LAVA_EDITOR=none
env COLD_LAVA_TODAY=2026-11-07
wait-for ☐ 16 open tasks
keys :
type list the open
wait-for list the open tasks by note
keys enter
wait-for ↑↓ move · x tick · ⏎ open
keys /
type two per
wait-for / two per▏
keys enter
wait-for 1 of 16 rows
keys j enter
wait-for whiteboard Volcano Venn · 5 cards
keys n
wait-for editing · type text · ⏎ new line · Esc done (saves)
type Draft
write Inbox/Chores.md - [ ] Sweep the ash off the roof\n
wait-for ☐ 17 open tasks
expect whiteboard Volcano Venn · 6 cards
expect Draft▏
screen
keys esc
wait-for open-tasks wanted to show a view: not while a card is being edited
expect-not Draft▏
screen
keys q
wait-for cold-lava workspaces
expect-not open-tasks wanted to show a view
screen
write Inbox/Chores.md - [ ] Sweep the ash off the roof\n- [ ] Count the masks\n
wait-for ☐ 18 open tasks
wait-for 1 of 17 rows · /two per
expect-not open-tasks wanted to show a view
keys esc
wait-for closed the list of open tasks
keys q
exits 0
